# Canonicalization

Environment: NixOS meta-distribution with nix flakes-enabled and preservation and a git repository in HOME with nix flakes-enabled git submodules in go-style paths that consist of a subset of numtide/blueprint directory structure.

# Initialize HOME
# Create the empty project remote
git_canonicalization init home
# Add required home whitelist entries in .gitignore
# Stage files before cleanup

# Initialize repository
git_canonicalization init flake git@github.com:owner/demo.git

# Add package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
git_canonicalization add python demo "A demo package."

# Remove package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
git_canonicalization rm demo

# Enter a development environment of a package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
nix develop .#<package-name>

# Run a local package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
nix run .#<package-name>

# Run an package from the registry
nix run nixpkgs#<package-name>

# Format, build/test packages/hosts
nix fmt
nix flake check

# Rules
# Use nix flakes in repositories
# git_canonicalization is solely responsible for persistent changes in the directory structure (prm/ is the escape hatch)
# prm/ directories must contain as few as possible
# tmp/ directories must be used to save artifacts
